        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "281a6653-6f60-570b-9930-0a7cc0062793",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Republican Party, GOP\n- Laws: Kansas–Nebraska Act, Missouri Compromise\n- People: Stephen A. Douglas, Franklin Pierce\n- Places: Kansas, Nebraska, Illinois\n- Events: Bleeding Kansas, Pottawatomie massacre\n- Concepts: popular sovereignty\n\nFacts:\n- The Republican Party, also called the GOP for \"Grand Old Party,\" emerged in 1854.\n- The Republican Party emerged to combat the Kansas–Nebraska Act.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act dissolved the terms of the Missouri Compromise.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act allowed slave or free status in the territories to be decided by popular sovereignty.\n- The Kansas–Nebraska Act created the territories of Kansas and Nebraska.\n- Democratic Senator Stephen A. Douglas of Illinois drafted the Kansas–Nebraska Act with President Franklin Pierce.\n- The Republican Party is one of the world's oldest extant political parties.\n- Bleeding Kansas was largely brought about by the Missouri Compromise and the Kansas–Nebraska Act.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
